    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Business-Operations-Manager--NJ-PBS-_R1005130": {
      "title": "Business Operations Manager (NJ PBS)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the General Manager, the Business Operations Manager provides operational and financial support to NJ PBS station leadership and departments. This position serves as the central resource for office operations, people processes, vendor management, and operational functions across the station. The Business Administrator ensures station operations run efficiently and supports the General Manager in managing day-to-day operations of the NJ PBS office. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Manage and monitor cost center budgets, grant accounts, and earned revenue accounts. Prepare and submit financial reports to the NJ PBS and other funders as needed. Oversee day-to-day budget operations while supporting the GM, who retains overall budget responsibility. Process purchase orders, invoices, and expense reports in coordination with university financial systems. Collaborate with Human Resources, Procurement, Facilities, and other University offices to manage comprehensive employee onboarding and cross-departmental operations, ensuring timely payroll, benefits enrollment, workspace allocation, and regulatory compliance. Manage vendor contracts and relationships ( including office supplies, equipment, and maintenance).). Serve as the point of contact for external vendors and service providers to monitor performance, resolve issues, and ensure compliance. Oversee office supply inventory and coordinate facility maintenance activities to ensure a safe, efficient, and well-equipped work environment. Support grant compliance documentation and record-keeping. Oversee the station master calendar, event scheduling, and internal communications. Manage and oversee all station travel operations and reimbursement workflows, enforcing compliance with University and grant travel policies, budgetary constraints, and documentation requirements. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in a related field. Minimum of two years of professional experience in an administrative role. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and Google Workspace. Excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills. Experience with various electronic databases and technology-dependent office operations, including Microsoft Office and Google Suite programs. Proven experience in project coordination and process improvement. Excellent organizational skills and self-initiative to perform a wide range of tasks without direct supervision or guidance. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects and demonstrate creativity, flexibility, self-motivation, and strong problem-solving, analysis, and communication skills. PREFERRED : Master’s degree from accredited college or university. Experience in a university, public media, or nonprofit administrative environment. Familiarity with Workday. Demonstrated experience in office administration or operational management, including financial administration, vendor management, and HR processes Familiarity with project management tools and document management systems. Familiarity with state and federal procurement laws. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $66,067.40-$85,903.70 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Subject-Area-Program-Data-Management-Specialist_R1005125": {
      "title": "Subject Area Program Data Management Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY:  Reporting to the Chair of the Department of Teaching and Learning, the Subject Area Program Data Management Specialist is a full-time position in an established and well-regarded teacher education program in the P-12 subject areas that prepares middle/secondary teachers with certifications in 17 subject areas across the MSU campus (e.g., mathematics, English, foreign languages, social studies, health/PE, art, music, dance, theater, the sciences, etc.). The Specialist works closely with the program faculty, Undergraduate Program Coordinator, Graduate Program Coordinator (GPC), and Clinical Course Coordinator, and has primary responsibility for managing clerical and administrative functions specific to the subject area programs. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Oversee data management for all aspects of the program, including collecting, organizing, and analyzing current and post-graduation data. Organize and track the subject area program course schedule, staffing, and room assignments. Process the hiring, onboarding, welcoming, and orientation of subject area adjunct faculty. Assist with the planning and management of annual academic program events such as Clinical Orientation and the Action Research Symposium, including organizing catering; reserving rooms; managing event RSVPs and sign-in; preparing programs and folders; organizing student schedules for individual sessions; processing speaker/presenter honoraria.  Manage the budget system to procure goods and services; arrange professional development credits for collaborating in-service teachers; and follow up with students who do not attend. Monitor the subject area program's web presence to ensure that it is current and accurate. Monitor enrollment data and provide regular updates to the program coordinators to balance course sections, hire additional instructors, and confirm instructors. Manage and monitor enrollment and student progress data in P12 clinical and seminar course sections; communicate with students and instructors as needed. Provide support for P12 accreditation and program approval activities. Visit clinical locations with the program coordinators for cooperating teacher information sessions and orientations. Process paperwork for P12 subject area preclinical placements and mentors. Track, schedule, and organize subject area adjunct observations. Organize and attend subject area GPC/UPC meetings; schedule meetings and rooms; prepare meeting materials; manage RSVPs, distribution of minutes, and meeting follow-up. Follow up consistently (i.e., weekly) on pending items related to scheduling, hiring, payment, reimbursement, etc. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS:   REQUIRED: Bachelor's degree in education or a related field. Minimum of three years of professional experience. Highly proficient in Microsoft Office suite, especially Excel/Google Sheets. Exceptional organizational and communication skills. Enthusiastic self-starter who can manage multiple priorities simultaneously within a dynamic higher education environment. PREFERRED:   Experience supporting colleagues and community and/or P-12 school partners. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $76,486.40-$84,131.83 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Teaching and Learning Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Manager-of-Grounds-and-Event-Services_R1005077": {
      "title": "Manager of Grounds and Event Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Director of Grounds, Moving and Event Support Services, the Manager of Grounds and Event Services oversees operational and administrative management of grounds and landscape maintenance, athletic fields, moving services and event set-ups. Working in collaboration with the Director, this position develops and recommends plans for program operation, assessment and improvement that support the institution’s mission and enhance the level of excellence for which Montclair State University is known.  The Manager of Grounds and Event Services manages daily operations related to outdoor maintenance, snow and ice removal, waste coordination, furniture and equipment moves, and event setup services; while ensuring compliance with established policies, safety regulations, and environmental standards.  This position additionally recommends and implements continuous improvement initiatives, upholds customer service excellence, and supports sustainability and efficiency goals across facilities operations. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Manage campus grounds maintenance, landscaping, and athletic fields in work that includes mowing, chemical treatments, renovations, irrigation, pruning, propagation, transplanting, waste removal, and snow removal.  Enforce grounds maintenance standards on a level commensurate with high-quality academic and student experiences. Collaborate and coordinate with campus stakeholders to plan and provide support services for moving events, programs, and activities that vary in scope and size. Supervise, train, schedule and evaluate supervisory and frontline staff. Monitor service quality, recommend and implement operational improvements to enhance efficiency and customer satisfaction. Develop and recommend policies and plans for the improved effectiveness of staff, equipment, materials and supplies. Assist with developing and managing operating budgets, contracts, inventories and procurement activities. Assist with coordinating emergency response and weather-related operations impacting campus grounds and events. Support division sustainability initiatives related to the work unit. Utilize the work management system to coordinate work, establish performance metrics and provide reports supporting decision-making. Assume responsibility for the overall operation of the Grounds, Fleet and Support Services work unit in the absence of the Director. Maintain knowledge of and compliance with applicable workplace safety guidelines and rules.  Attend occupational and professional training as directed and enforce health and safety training directives with staff. Represent the University at conferences or meetings and serve on ad hoc and standing committees as required. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Professional certification in Grounds Management. Minimum five years of hands-on Grounds operations experience, including three years of supervisory experience with fiscal and performance management responsibilities. A valid driver’s license. Technical knowledge and understanding of grounds management practices, including snow and ice removal, horticultural procedures and equipment operation. Experience using maintenance management systems. Ability to work during snow events and institutionally significant activities outside of standard business hours. Ability to work when the campus is closed, or due to delayed opening or early closure. PREFERRED : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. NJ Pesticide Applicator’s License (license will be required within 6 months of hire). Experience maintaining grounds at an institution of higher education. Working knowledge of APPA standards and service levels related to grounds and project management. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $95,000.00-$105,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Moving Services Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/HR-Benefits-Coordinator--Temporary-_R1005103": {
      "title": "HR Benefits Coordinator (Temporary)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nPart time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY Reporting to the Director of Benefits, the HR Benefits Coordinator performs administrative support of the day-to-day operations for administering the benefits, leave of absence, ADA, and workers' compensation programs. * *This is a Temporary assignment with a minimum of 35 hours per week and will commence immediately. The initial, anticipated duration of the assignment is approximately 3 months with the possibility of extension.** PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Primarily responsible for the administration of benefits including but not limited to health, prescription, dental, flexible spending, life insurance, pension and retirement benefits, ACA, COBRA, employee tuition program, leave of absence, ADA, wellness benefits, unemployment claims and workers' compensation. Tracks, communicates and processes health enrollments for individuals offered coverage in compliance with the Affordable Care Act. Reviews and responds to unemployment claims inquiries with the appropriate information and documentation. Maintains employee benefits filing systems Ensures benefits changes are entered appropriately in the payroll system for payroll deductions. Prepares and facilitates Employee Benefits workshops•Maintains and prepares biweekly employee payroll reports. Reviews all medical documentation and work-related accident reports for completeness and clarity of data to ensure compliance with policy and regulatory requirements. Serves as a liaison between employees and the State to resolves benefit related issues. Audits reports to ensure accurate benefit elections, eligibility, and deductions for employees and their covered dependents. Maintains open communication with the Payroll Department to ensure specified deadlines are met. Ensures compliance with federal and State laws, including reporting requirements. Serves as point of contact for retiree medical and retirement questions Manages vision benefit reimbursement program, including verifying eligibility, reviewing supporting documentation and requesting reimbursement through payroll. Assists in conducting new hire orientations, annual open enrollment and maintaining benefits orientation materials. Communicates and interacts with medical professionals, support agencies and others to monitor and assess employees' progress returning to work from leave of absence. Manages leave of absence process in Workday by monitoring leave balances and keeping track of used and unused balances; provides Workday support for employees on leave, as well as their supervisors. Manages workflow to ensure all employees on leave payroll transactions are processed accurately and timely. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. ​ QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor's degree from accredited college or university. A minimum of three years of employee benefits related administration experience. Knowledge and working experience with pertinent federal and State regulations affecting employee benefit programs, including OSHA, COBRA, ACA, FMLA, NJFLA, ADA. ​ PREFERRED : Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. Working experience with the NJ State systems (MBOS, PMIS, EPIC). Proficiency in MS Office Suite (Outlook, Excel, Word and PowerPoint).•Ability to manage several projects simultaneously while working under pressure to meet deadlines. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Exceptional organization and customer service skills. Strong analytical and problem resolution skills. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.  Salary Range $30.00-$35.00 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Employee Benefits (Temporary) Position Type Hourly - Temporary Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Engineering_R1005099": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Physics and Astronomy at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Engineering position to begin August 2027. This position will contribute to the launch of a new Engineering concentration and support the development of the corresponding curriculum.  The ideal applicant will have strong familiarity and experience with the standard curricula for physics and at least one core engineering discipline (especially Mechanical, Aerospace, Electrical, Optical, or Nuclear Engineering). Other engineering or physics disciplines may also be considered. The applicant’s research area should likewise connect with an engineering discipline or a related area of physics or applied physics. The successful candidate is expected to develop a robust, self-directed research agenda capable of attracting external funding (startup funding will be available). They will be able to teach a combination of introductory physics courses, advanced laboratory courses, and specialized upper-level engineering and physics electives. The new faculty will actively mentor undergraduate physics majors, provide advising for career paths in engineering and physics, and offer research opportunities that help students prepare for graduate programs and industry jobs. They will also contribute to departmental growth, curriculum design, and other department service commitments. The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) per semester. The University supports research excellence through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. THE DEPARTMENT OF PHYSICS AND ASTRONOMY The Department of Physics and Astronomy at Montclair State University was formed in 2018 and consists of 7 faculty members and well over 100 physics majors. Our students represent a diverse population and include many first-generation college students. In addition to a major and minor in Physics, we also offer a concentration in astronomy and several dual-degree options, including a 3+2 BS Physics + Master’s in Mechanical Engineering with Stevens Institute of Technology. Additional 3+2 dual-degree options involving physics and engineering, as well as an engineering concentration, are under active consideration. Multiple teacher certification pathways are also available. Along with a commitment to effective teaching, research excellence and student involvement in research are key components of our department’s culture. Our faculty are active and internationally recognized in the disciplines of gravitational-wave physics, astrophysics, optics, and nuclear physics. Current facilities include two introductory teaching labs, a dedicated lab for upper-level physics courses, a machining/fabrication shop, and dedicated research labs focusing on optics and low-energy nuclear physics. Other lab facilities available on campus include NMR, AFM, TEM, and ICP-MS. A new interdisciplinary science building (expected to open in 2028) will further expand our teaching and research spaces. The department strives to create an atmosphere of collegiality, inclusion, and the promotion of excellence. Additional information about our Department can be found online at  https://inside.montclair.edu/colleges-schools-research/math-science/physics-and-astronomy-department   THE COLLEGE OF SCIENCE AND MATHEMATICS The College of Science and Mathematics at Montclair State University empowers the next generation of STEM leaders through rigorous academics, hands-on discovery, and inclusive excellence. Our mission is grounded in a student-centered philosophy that values the dedication of our faculty, the curiosity of our students, and a shared commitment to advancing scientific knowledge and innovation. With modern facilities and cutting-edge technology, we offer distinctive undergraduate and graduate programs across the Departments of Biology, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Earth and Environmental Studies, Mathematics, and Physics and Astronomy and the School of Computing. Through a research-driven curriculum, community-engaged learning, and real-world problem-solving experiences, CSAM equips students with durable skill sets to meet the demands of an evolving world. By cultivating strong partnerships with industry, government, and nonprofit organizations, the College drives economic growth, advances environmental sustainability, and strengthens the STEM workforce across New Jersey and beyond. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: A PhD in Engineering (Mechanical, Aerospace, Electrical, Optical, Nuclear), Physics, Applied Physics, or closely related fields.  A proven track record of peer-reviewed publications and a competitive research agenda with clear potential for external funding and that can substantially involve undergraduate students. Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching physics and engineering courses, which readily translates to the Montclair State student body. Demonstrated interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: Prior experience in teaching, working in industry, or postdoctoral research. STARTING DATE:  August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter that briefly summarizes your qualifications, explains your interest in joining our department, and discusses your vision for contributing to an engineering concentration at Montclair. Complete curriculum vitae. Research Statement (3 to 5 pages) highlighting your research accomplishments, current field of interest, planned future directions or aspirations, potential sources of external funding, and plans for involving undergraduate students. Teaching statement (2 to 4 pages) that addresses: (i) your overall approach to teaching; (ii) successful pedagogical strategies for a student population with diverse backgrounds and levels of preparation; and (iii) courses that you envision teaching at Montclair. Contact information for three to five references, including name, title, affiliation, email, and phone. The search committee will solicit references directly following an initial screening of applicants. APPLY BY:    Applications should be submitted by December 1, 2026 to ensure full consideration. Initial screening will begin shortly thereafter and be complete by the end of December. On-campus interviews are expected to take place in February 2027. The position is open until filled. Questions about this position can be directed to physics-search@montclair.edu . Salary Range $100,398.29-$116,469.62 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Physics and Astronomy Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Mathematics_R1005101": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Mathematics at Montclair State University invites applications for a 10-month Assistant Teaching Professor position. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in foundational mathematics education, a critical priority for the College. Primary responsibilities include instruction and instructional support for MATH 108 (Transition to College Mathematics) and MATH 111 (Precalculus) to address evolving student needs and increasing enrollment.             Teaching Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching and service. Position is a two-year, ten-month, non-tenure track appointment, with eligibility for reappointment based on established NTTP procedures. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for 10-month teaching faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with an option for additional 6 TCH in the summer for a 12-month faculty appointment.  Reassigned time (course release) is available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as administering programs. Teaching Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Service : Teaching Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, and university. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University.  THE DEPARTMENT OF MATHEMATICS The Department of Mathematics, housed in the College of Science and Mathematics (CSAM), is committed to excellence in teaching, learning, scholarship, and service to the mathematics and mathematics education communities. We offer a variety of programs ranging from undergraduate and graduate degrees in mathematics and mathematics education to a PhD in mathematics education. Our students are prepared for careers in mathematics and beyond, as well as continued education at the graduate level. Department activities range from undergraduate and graduate instruction to research. Faculty conduct theoretical, applied, and social science research, often in collaboration with colleagues and students. Our professional activities in research, education and consulting extend to the local, regional, national and international level. The department creates an atmosphere in which a diverse community of students and faculty recognize, explore and promote the importance, power, and beauty of the mathematical sciences. THE COLLEGE OF SCIENCE AND MATHEMATICS The College of Science and Mathematics at Montclair State University empowers the next generation of STEM leaders through rigorous academics, hands-on discovery, and inclusive excellence. Our mission is grounded in a student-centered philosophy that values the dedication of our faculty, the curiosity of our students, and a shared commitment to advancing scientific knowledge and innovation. With modern facilities and cutting-edge technology, we offer distinctive undergraduate and graduate programs across the Departments of Biology, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Earth and Environmental Studies, Mathematics, and Physics and Astronomy, and the School of Computing. Through a research-driven curriculum, community-engaged learning, and real-world problem-solving experiences, CSAM equips students with durable skill sets to meet the demands of an evolving world. By cultivating strong partnerships with industry, government, and nonprofit organizations, the College drives economic growth, advances environmental sustainability, and strengthens the STEM workforce across New Jersey and beyond. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: PhD (or equivalent) in Mathematics, Mathematics Education, or closely related field. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive teaching. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. STARTING DATE: August 27, 2027  REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, and teaching and service statements which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates should be prepared to supply 3 letters of recommendation. APPLY BY: The position is open until filled, and application review begins December 1, 2026. Salary Range $82,597.65-$92,515.81 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Mathematics Position Type Teaching Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Computational-Biology_R1005100": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Computational Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION :  Montclair State University, Department of Biology, offers an exciting opportunity for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Computational Biology beginning in August of 2027. We seek a colleague whose interests include teaching introductory and advanced Computational Biology, establishing a vigorous, extramurally funded research program that involves both graduate and undergraduate students, and which will support new programs that are being developed, such as an online M.S. in Computational Biology. We are particularly interested in qualified candidates who can contribute, through their research, teaching, and service, to the diversity and excellence of the academic community.  Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching: The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.   Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity: Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service: Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  DEPARTMENT DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Biology has a collaborative culture in which tenured and tenure-track faculty members work together to support student learning. It integrates everything from molecular biology to ecosystems biology within the department and incorporates the multiple institutes, centers, departments, and schools within the College of Science and Mathematics. From the use of the next generation sequencing and organismal genetic modification to the development of field sites around the world, the Department goals are to expand our understanding of living systems and to foster a critical-thinking mentality at all levels. The student population reflects the diversity of the university as a whole, with 55% students in the department coming from groups generally underrepresented in the sciences. SCHOOL DESCRIPTION The College of Science and Mathematics at Montclair State University empowers the next generation of STEM leaders through rigorous academics, hands-on discovery, and inclusive excellence. Our mission is grounded in a student-centered philosophy that values the dedication of our faculty, the curiosity of our students, and a shared commitment to advancing scientific knowledge and innovation. With modern facilities and cutting-edge technology, we offer distinctive undergraduate and graduate programs across the Departments of Biology, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Earth and Environmental Studies, Mathematics, and Physics and Astronomy, and the School of Computing. Through a research-driven curriculum, community-engaged learning, and real-world problem-solving experiences, CSAM equips students with durable skill sets to meet the demands of an evolving world. By cultivating strong partnerships with industry, government, and nonprofit organizations, the College drives economic growth, advances environmental sustainability, and strengthens the STEM workforce across New Jersey and beyond. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: A Ph.D. in Computational Biology or a relevant field is required. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: Significant record of scholarly/creative work.  STARTING DATE:     August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $99,422.70-$116,469.62 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Biology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Reporter--Trenton-Central-Jersey_R1004985": {
      "title": "Reporter, Trenton/Central Jersey",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the News Director, the Reporter, Trenton/Central New Jersey, serves as NJ PBS's statehouse and capital correspondent, covering the New Jersey Legislature, Governor's office, state agencies, and policy developments from Trenton. This individual provides in-depth political and policy reporting for broadcast, streaming, and digital platforms and serves as a key resource for NJ PBS's government accountability journalism. In addition, this position also covers news in Central New Jersey, including Union, Somerset, Hunterdon, Mercer, Middlesex, and Monmouth counties. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Cover the New Jersey Legislature, Governor's office, and state agencies on a daily basis. Develop political and policy enterprise stories with depth and context. Cover news in Central New Jersey. Attend and report on press conferences, committee hearings, and floor sessions. File content for daily newscasts and digital platforms on deadline. Contribute to the booking of guests and interview subjects. Participate in editorial meetings, pitch stories and ideas for coverage, and contribute to story selection and news judgment. Write and produce video packages for broadcast and digital distribution. Maintain close working relationships with statehouse sources, press offices, and policy experts. Contribute to political analysis and special coverage, including elections, the state budget, and legislative sessions. May substitute-anchor on news programs from time to time as needed. Represent NJ PBS in the Statehouse press corps and at related events and community events in the Central New Jersey coverage area. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time.   QUALIFICATIONS:  REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in journalism, communications, broadcasting, or a related field.  A minimum of three years of video-based reporting experience, including field reporting, and clip and package production. Knowledge of state legislative and executive branch processes. Ability to shoot and edit video content for broadcast and digital delivery. Valid NJ driver’s license. Experience with digital and social media storytelling. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines.   PREFERRED: Prior New Jersey Statehouse or political reporting experience Deep familiarity with New Jersey’s political landscape and policy environment Experience with data journalism or public records analysis Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $80,000.00-$95,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
