    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor-Economics_R1005078": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor-Economics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION: The Economics Department at Montclair State University seeking to hire an Applied Empirical Economist with expertise in conducting rigorous, data-driven research that informs public policy and decision-making. This position offers the opportunity to conduct high-impact research that contributes to evidence-based policies aimed at improving economic opportunity, health outcomes, housing affordability, and equitable access to emerging technologies. The successful candidate is expected to investigate how artificial intelligence (AI) and emerging technologies are transforming public policy, with particular attention to their impact on areas such as community development, health care, and affordable housing. The candidate should demonstrate an interest in leveraging innovative analytical tools and interdisciplinary approaches to address complex policy challenges. The successful candidate will be expected to establish a strong, externally funded research program by securing competitive grants and contracts from federal agencies, foundations, and other funding organizations. They should demonstrate the potential to build collaborative partnerships across disciplines and with community, government, and industry stakeholders to advance impactful, policy-relevant research. Teaching: The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity: Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service: Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. THE DEPARTMENT OF ECONOMICS: The Department of Economics offers a BA in Economics, a minor in Economics, and a concentration in Asset Management. Separately, the department supports the MBA Program in teaching both required and elective graduate level courses in economics. As the department has a rich portfolio of programs, we seek candidates who can be effective in teaching across all programs -- both introductory and advanced courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The candidate selected is expected to pursue scholarly research leading to publications in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals and conference proceedings and increase the visibility of the economics department by developing relationships with external stakeholders. In addition, the candidate is expected to serve on department, school, and university-level committees, advise students, and participate in curriculum review and development activities. THE FELICIANO SCHOOL OF BUSINESS The Feliciano School of Business is committed to transforming today’s students into tomorrow’s business leaders through innovative teaching, experiential learning, and strong industry engagement. Accredited by AACSB International, the School offers distinctive programs at both the undergraduate and graduate programs, including the BS in Business Analytics, BS in Business Administration (eight concentrations), BS in Accounting, BA in Economics, BA in Hospitality, Sports, Events and Tourism, MBA, MS in Accounting, MS in Business Analytics, MS in Digital Marketing Analytics, and MS in Human Resource Analytics, as well as a range of minors and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Among the School’s strengths are its world-class faculty and staff, diverse and driven student body, engaged alumni network, and strong corporate and institutional partnerships. Both academic and program-related activities are focused on student success and experiential learning beyond the classroom. The Ellyn A. McColgan Center for Student Services further supports students through results-driven advising, career guidance, and access to internships, co-ops, and mentorship opportunities that help prepare them for success in today’s dynamic business environment. The School is also home to the Feliciano Center for Entrepreneurship + Innovation, a collaborative community that supports innovation and entrepreneurship through mentorship, strategic guidance, and opportunities that help students and entrepreneurs develop and grow their ideas. Nearly 120 full-time faculty members and 41 professional staff, with terminal degrees and advanced training from leading universities, bring a wealth of academic and industry expertise to the School. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: ● Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree. ● Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. ● Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. ● A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED ● Significant record of scholarly/creative work. STARTING DATE August 27, 2027 REQUIRED MATERIALS Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process. Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY: The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $112,451.79-$124,505.29 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Economics Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Criminal-Justice_R1005049": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies/School of Social Sciences/College of Humanities and Social Sciences POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies at Montclair State University is actively seeking applications for an Assistant Professor in Criminal Justice to begin in August 2027. For this tenure-track appointment, we are engaging in a broad search in any area of criminal justice or criminology, however, we are particularly searching for professors ready to offer courses in our required sequence, including research methods, criminology, and/or the department’s interdisciplinary course on theories of justice. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.  . Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. . Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  THE DEPARTMENT OF SOCIOLOGY, CRIMINOLOGY, AND JUSTICE STUDIES:  The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies is the second largest department in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences.  Our criminal justice concentration alone has over five hundred enrolled majors.  We also offer a master’s degree in Justice Innovation and Leadership.  Featuring dynamic faculty from a variety of disciplines, our interdisciplinary focus includes Criminal Justice/Criminology, Law, International Justice, and Social Justice. Justice Studies serves a large minoritized and first generation college student population. Our faculty are dedicated to providing support and guidance for our students, as well as a robust education experience to prepare them for the workforce. THE COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES:  The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Sociology, or a related field. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Significant record of scholarly/creative work.  Experience teaching criminology, criminal justice, or sociology courses at the undergraduate level. Experience teaching a diverse student body and first generation college students. Peer-reviewed publications in criminology, criminal justice, or a related field. STARTING DATE      August 27, 2027      REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately.   APPLY BY :   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $76,486.40-$100,398.29 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Senior-Producer_R1004935": {
      "title": "Executive Producer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the News Director, the Executive Producer is responsible for NJ PBS's news content across all platforms, including broadcast programs, digital content, live streaming, and live coverage. This position plans and executes the daily news broadcasts that air on NJ PBS, including a weeknight evening newscast, a weekday news interview talk show, and any special broadcast coverage of planned events or breaking news. This position also oversees the planning and editorial direction of content on digital platforms and live streaming channels.  The Executive Producer works closely with the News Director to balance breaking news (on digital and/or linear platforms) with planned coverage.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Build and manage the daily rundown and oversee the live production of video-based news programs — including those for the nightly newscast and other broadcast programs, digital platforms, and special event coverage — selecting and ordering stories for maximum editorial impact. Time scripts and segments to appropriate length depending on platform.  Coordinate with the assignment desk, reporters, anchors, and technical staff to ensure all elements are ready before they are posted or aired.  Write and edit scripts and promos for daily programs. Assist in developing future NJ PBS live-streaming channels. Track story progress and production deadlines, alerting producers, reporters,  and editors when deadlines are at risk.  Adapt coverage plans in response to breaking news, re-stacking rundowns and coordinating live coverage as needed. Review reporter packages and edited content before it is posted or aired, checking for accuracy, fairness, and technical quality. Oversee the planning and execution of news content on all digital platforms. Supervise the Producer, Digital Content; the V-Mix Operator; and the Graphics Producer and Editor to ensure seamless content delivery across broadcast, digital, and live streaming platforms.   Work closely with the News Director to develop coverage strategies, establish editorial priorities, and ensure consistency across NJ PBS news platforms. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. ​ QUALIFICATIONS :  REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in journalism, communications, broadcasting, or a related field.  Minimum of four years of experience in broadcast news production, including rundown management, live newscast and special event program execution. Demonstrated experience in digital news content production on multiple platforms. Proficiency with newsroom management systems and broadcast production tools. Ability to work under deadline pressure in a fast-paced live news environment. Strong background in journalism. PREFERRED: Experience at a news media organization or PBS-affiliated station. Familiarity with the New Jersey news landscape Experience with digital-first and multiplatform newscast workflows Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $95,000.00-$120,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Change-Management-Director--Workday---System-Enhancements_R1005072": {
      "title": "Change Management Director, Workday & System Enhancements",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Director of PMO Operations, The Change Manager leads organizational change initiatives by developing and executing strategies that enable successful adoption of new processes, systems, and ways of working. This role partners with project teams, business leaders, and stakeholders to minimize disruption, build organizational readiness, and ensure employees are equipped to embrace change. Success in this role requires strong communication, stakeholder engagement, training, and change management expertise to drive sustainable business outcomes. This position is expected to work onsite and/or in a hybrid work arrangement based on business and operational needs. The position requires regular on-campus presence, as determined by the department and the needs of the role. **Continued employment in this position is contingent upon the project's duration, workload needs, and available funding. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and execute organizational change management strategies, processes, and tools that enable successful adoption of project and business initiatives across the organization. Create and implement comprehensive change management plans that align with project objectives, organizational priorities, and business transformation goals. Assess organizational readiness and evaluate the impact of planned changes on employees, leaders, business processes, and overall organizational performance. Identify, assess, and mitigate organizational, operational, and people-related risks associated with change initiatives throughout the project lifecycle. Identify, manage, and address anticipated resistance to change through proactive engagement, coaching, and targeted stakeholder support strategies. Partner with leadership to define employee roles, responsibilities, and organizational impacts resulting from business and technology transformation initiatives. Develop and execute communication strategies that clearly explain upcoming changes, business impacts, and actions required to support successful adoption. Design, coordinate, and deliver training programs, learning materials, and job aids that prepare employees and managers for organizational change. Conduct stakeholder assessments to identify key influencers, sponsors, and impacted groups critical to successful implementation and long-term adoption. Establish change success metrics, monitor adoption and readiness, analyze results, and recommend corrective actions to improve business outcomes. Lead change management workstreams using structured methodologies while providing regular status updates, reporting, and recommendations to leadership and project teams. Identify training needs across stakeholder groups and coordinate training logistics, schedules, resources, and delivery to support successful implementation. Perform other related duties as assigned. Management retains the right to change or add job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Minimum five (5) years of progressive professional experience in IT management, large-scale transformation projects, or related field. Demonstrated success in rolling out ERP systems-preferably Workday- in a university setting, with a track record of stakeholder engagement and high adoption rates. Demonstrated expertise in planning and facilitating organizational change. Strong knowledge of organizational change management principles, methodologies, techniques, and industry best practices. Excellent stakeholder engagement, relationship management, and influencing skills across all organizational levels. Ability to manage multiple priorities and perform effectively in fast-paced environments. PREFERRED : Master’s degree from an accredited university. Additional related certifications (e.g., CAPM, PMP, or Scrum Master). Formal Change Management certification (ProSci. PMI-ACP, or similar) Deep understanding of higher education operational structures, processes, and accreditation requirements. Expertise in stakeholder engagement, conflict resolution, and overseeing cross-departmental training initiatives. Proficiency with project management and collaboration tools (e.g., Smartsheet, Microsoft Project, or Jira). Certification in Parliamentary Procedures and Proceedings for Governance. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $125,000.00-$135,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department PMO Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Associate-Director-of-Strategic-Sourcing_R1005075": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Strategic Sourcing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Procurement Services, the Associate Director of Strategic Sourcing is responsible for developing and managing sourcing templates, gathering and analyzing data, conducting market research, and providing insights to support strategic sourcing initiatives. This role collaborates with cross-functional teams, negotiates with suppliers, and analyzes market trends to make informed purchasing decisions that best meet the needs of Montclair State University. This position also provides recommendations to improve procedures, policies, and specifications to formulate a strong and effective sourcing approach. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop complex formal solicitations for various procurements for goods and services to meet the University's needs utilizing market research as necessary to incorporate best practices. Lead collaboration with stakeholders and University departments on solicitations to understand business needs and to review their existing and anticipated requirements. Manage the entire bid process including developing bid schedules, conducting pre-bid meetings, reviewing and analyzing technical information accompanying bids to determine specification compliance, participating as a voting member of the technical evaluation committee as determined, presenting a recommendation to award, and drafting the necessary agreements and follows through to contract execution. Develop and maintain sourcing templates. Supervise sourcing staff and mentor other members of the Procurement Services Department in the development of formal solicitation processes and other strategic sourcing tasks, as requested and assisted. Recruit, hire, train, develop, and evaluate direct reports. Implement contract administration procedures and provide training instructing departments on their responsibilities for newly awarded contracts. Create effective processes for routinely informing leadership about project status, workload, constraints, and pipeline prioritization. Perform spend analysis for the University as well as specific commodity areas, provide recommendations on sourcing strategy, and deliver savings to the University. This may include preparing specifications for RFPs that can be utilized by the entire university community as well as areas for cost-saving opportunities. Responsible for ensuring additional compliant mechanisms and contracts are created that will make procuring items easier for the community Engage with stakeholders and University departments to convey policies, confirm requests, advise on anticipated requirements, and foster better communication and improvement of service. Provide advice on the supplier selection process, preferred suppliers, and the overall procurement process. Utilize various key performance indicators such as forecasts, variances, and other reporting tools to evaluate supplier and initiative performance. Maintain supplier performance and relationships and serve as the escalation point for supplier performance issues. Analyze procurement costs and develop cost reduction strategies while tracking savings. Review and propose policies and processes as they relate to job responsibilities. Support the development and implementation of strategic initiatives and process improvements while ensuring compliance. Maintain a complete understanding of the Montclair State University Act, New Jersey State, and Federal rules, laws, and regulations, University policies concerning and ensure compliance with all. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Minimum 4 years of professional experience with the procurement process in a large organization. Knowledge of strategic sourcing and specification development skills. Commitment to the principles and practices of continuous improvement. Strong technology skills and analytical capabilities. Ability to adapt and innovate while adhering to established procedures. Strengths as a self-initiative and a self-motivated. Ability to work independently and to collaborate with others. PREFERRED : Master’s degree from an accredited university in a relevant field. Professional leadership experience with the procurement process in a large organization. Specific knowledge as it pertains to specification development, Request for Proposal preparation, the public bid process, contract preparation, and administration. Familiarity with New Jersey procurement statutes and regulations. Prefer experience with Workday, the University’s ERP system. Management experience is strongly preferred. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $130,000.00-$145,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Procurement Services Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Athletic-Training_R1005046": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Athletic Training",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Kinesiology in the College for Community Health at Montclair State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Athletic Training, beginning August 27, 2027. We seek a faculty member whose teaching, research, and professional engagement advance the field of Athletic Training and contribute to the preparation of future healthcare professionals. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, injury prevention, clinical biomechanics, rehabilitation, therapeutic interventions, sport and human performance, emergency care, health and wellness, or other areas relevant to Athletic Training education and practice. The successful candidate will contribute to creating an engaging and supportive learning environment for the undergraduate and graduate programs in Athletic Training and Kinesiology and play an important role in preparing students for professional practice through classroom, laboratory, and clinical education experiences. Applicants should demonstrate potential for impactful scholarship, excellence in teaching, and a commitment to student mentorship and success. The ability to engage in interdisciplinary collaboration, interprofessional education, and community-engaged scholarship is highly desirable. As part of the College for Community Health, the successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty across health-related disciplines and contribute to initiatives that promote health, wellness, and quality of life in diverse populations. In addition, the candidate is expected to contribute to service activities at the department, college, and university levels; maintain an active scholarly agenda; support accreditation and program assessment activities; and engage with healthcare, athletic, educational, and community partners throughout the region. The successful candidate will join a collaborative department committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service, with access to the extensive healthcare, sport, and professional opportunities available throughout the New York metropolitan area. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. THE DEPARTMENT OF KINESIOLOGY The Department of Kinesiology at Montclair State University is dedicated to preparing future leaders in athletic training, physical education, exercise science, sport administration, coaching, and related professions through innovative undergraduate and graduate education. The department advances the University’s mission by educating highly skilled professionals, fostering scholarship and community engagement, and developing partnerships that address workforce needs across healthcare, educational, sport, and corporate settings. Through nationally recognized and accredited programs, including a CAATE-accredited Athletic Training program, hands-on clinical and experiential learning opportunities, and a commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service, the department prepares graduates to improve health, safety, physical activity, athletic performance, and quality of life in diverse communities. Faculty are committed to student success, interdisciplinary collaboration, and advancing evidence-based practice across the health, sport, and performance professions. THE COLLEGE FOR COMMUNITY HEALTH The College for Community Health (CCHL) at Montclair State University is dedicated to addressing pressing health inequities in New Jersey, the region, and beyond. We are dedicated to furthering the Montclair State University mission by educating and preparing students to meet the needs of the health workforce; engaging with communities and the public to improve health services, systems, and outcomes, and developing meaningful inquiry and scholarship in and for health. In synergy with existing groups and organizations, leveraging the university's strengths, and expanding academic offerings to meet critical health workforce needs, CCHL is leading the way to healthier people and communities, establishing itself as a key transformational leader in the New Jersey region and beyond. CCHL faculty are committed to interprofessional education and student engagement, with three priority areas: maternal and child health, wellness, and healthy aging across our 7 academic departments.           QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree (or ABD with degree completed by date of appointment) in Athletic Training, Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Rehabilitation Sciences, Health Sciences, or a closely related field. Board of Certification (BOC) credential in good standing as a Certified Athletic Trainer. Eligibility for licensure as an Athletic Trainer in the State of New Jersey. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: Significant record of scholarly/creative work. Previous teaching experience in an Athletic Training program or related health professions with special interest in CAATE-accredited experience, clinical education, preceptor development, and student supervision. Experience integrating simulation, technology, or innovative instructional methods into teaching. Expertise in one or more areas such as: Injury prevention Rehabilitation and therapeutic interventions Clinical biomechanics Emergency care (including BLS CPR/AED instructor certification) Sport performance Manual therapy Health promotion and wellness Healthcare administration Athletic Training pedagogy Evidence of interdisciplinary or interprofessional collaboration. Demonstrated ability or potential to develop partnerships with healthcare systems, secondary schools, collegiate athletics programs, or other clinical sites. Demonstrated ability to foster an inclusive learning environment that supports student success. Interest in securing external funding and contributing to community-engaged scholarship, service, or collaborative research initiatives. Previous experience with program assessment, accreditation, or curriculum development.            STARTING DATE                August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process. Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately.   APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $69,373.45-$108,433.95 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Kinesiology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Health-Psychology_R1005038": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Health Psychology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-01\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of Psychology/School of Behavioral and Cognitive Sciences/College of Humanities and Social Sciences/School POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Psychology at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, non-tenure track, Assistant Teaching Professor position in Health Psychology, beginning in August 2027. We seek a dynamic and collaborative colleague whose expertise in Health Psychology will contribute to a coordinated departmental initiative to expand Health Psychology across undergraduate, graduate, and online programs. This position represents an exciting opportunity to join one of the largest psychology departments in the region and to play a central role in building a distinctive Health Psychology presence that integrates research, education, and community impact. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Health Psychology and related areas and will serve as a key contributor to the development, assessment, and improvement of Health Psychology curricula and programs. The position offers opportunities to collaborate with faculty on innovative instructional initiatives, experiential learning opportunities, and community partnerships that enhance student success and career readiness. The Department of Psychology values an inclusive, student-centered academic environment, and seeks colleagues who demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, mentorship, and advising, as well as a dedication to engaging and supporting a diverse student population.  The position is a two-year, ten-month, non-tenure track (NTT) appointment, with eligibility for reappointment based on established NTT procedures. Montclair is committed to the success of teaching faculty through opportunities for promotion and professional development to support long-term success and flourishing at the University.  Teaching Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching and service. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for 10-month teaching faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with an additional 6 TCH in the summer for 12-month faculty.  Additional TCH reassigned time (course release) is available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as administering programs. Teaching Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Service : Teaching Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which teaching faculty members receive course release. DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGY The Psychology Department—organized into the three broad categories of clinical, industrial/organizational (I/O), and psychological science—serves a large and diverse constituency of students, and comprises a vibrant group of 35 full-time faculty, in addition to several emeriti faculty and support staff. The Department continues to expand its national profile, with 20 active research labs, over 3.5 million dollars in extramural funding, and PhD programs in both clinical and I/O psychology—in addition to popular MA and certification programs in clinical psychology, I/O psychology, psychological science, and advanced quantitative methods. The research interests of our faculty include neuroscience, neurodegenerative diseases, and neurocognitive aging; cognitive processes such as memory, the brain reward system, decision-making, perceptual processing, and spatial cognition; internalizing psychological disorders and trauma; forensic investigation, plea bargaining, and forensic and correctional assessment and treatment; language and life span development; motivation; pedagogy; effective leadership, mentorship, and supervision; organizational behavior; employee well-being, aging, and longevity; emotions and ethics in the workplace; and social attitudes, discrimination, diversity science, and social justice. COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned PhD in Psychology Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED : Preferred candidates will have a PhD in health psychology or a closely related subfield, with demonstrated excellence in teaching. We are open to subareas of specialization, and welcome candidates whose work addresses contemporary challenges in health and well-being, including behavioral health, chronic disease management, health equity, prevention science, aging, stress and resilience, digital health, and social determinants of health. Consideration will also be given to candidates who complement existing Department strengths in clinical psychology and I/O psychology.    STARTING DATE       August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae and teaching and service statements which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. Questions about the search can be addressed to Dr. John Paul Wilson: wilsonjoh@montclair.edu   APPLY BY :    The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $66,067.40-$95,821.86 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Psychology Position Type Teaching Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
