    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Latinx-Studies-and-Creative-Writing_R1005048": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Latinx Studies and Creative Writing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of English and Department of Global Cultural Studies/School for the Humanities/College of Humanities and Social Sciences POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of English and the Department of Global Cultural Studies at Montclair State University, a Hispanic-Serving Institution just 14 miles outside of New York City, are offering a joint tenure-track position in Latinx Studies and Creative Writing at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 2027. We invite PhD and MFA holders to send applications. We are especially interested in candidates capable of teaching creative writing workshops, courses in our Latin American and Latino Studies program, and English courses. The candidate’s area of expertise should be informed by immigration from the Caribbean and/or Latin America, dealing with such concepts as bilingualism, borders, and social justice. The candidate must have the oral and written proficiency necessary to teach in both English and Spanish and demonstrate a robust record or exceptional promise in terms of publishing academic articles, poetry, fiction, or other genres in Spanish. The successful candidate may also be asked to collaborate with other departments’ cross-listed courses and to lead interdisciplinary initiatives. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.  . Research , Scholarship, and Creative Activity: Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  DEPARTMENT OF ENGLISH and DEPARTMENT OF GLOBAL CULTURAL STUDIES The Department of English comprises more than 20 full-time faculty, over 300 undergraduate majors, and approximately 30 M.A. students; a diverse and wide-ranging literary studies curriculum is complemented by robust programs in creative writing, film studies, and teacher education. With more than 25 full-time faculty members, nearly 200 undergraduate majors across its programs, and approximately 30 M.A. students (Spanish and French), the Department of Global Cultural Studies is devoted to the study of global languages, literature, translation, cultural expression, religion, and Indigenous and Latino experiences. The department's interdisciplinary approach fosters linguistic and cultural literacy while advancing scholarship, research, and engagement across local and global communities.  THE COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Significant record of scholarly/creative work.  STARTING DATE     August 27, 2027      REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately.   APPLY BY :   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately.     Salary Range $76,486.40-$100,398.29 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department English Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Management_R1005054": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-31\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION : The Feliciano School of Business at Montclair State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Organizational Change and the Future of Work , starting on August 27, 2027. The Department of Management seeks a scholar whose research and teaching examines how organizations anticipate, lead, and adapt to major changes in work, technology, structure, and talent systems, including topics such as organizational change, change leadership, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, and human-technology collaboration.   The successful candidate will contribute to both undergraduate and graduate programs in management, entrepreneurship, human resources, and project management, and play a key role in developing innovative, future-focused courses such as Organizational Change and Development, Future of Work, Digital Transformation and Change Leadership, Leadership in Technology-Enabled Organizations, Human and AI Collaboration, and Workforce Analytics.  Scholarly focus and agenda should include organizational change, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, or related technology-enabled changes in management. The ability to engage in interdisciplinary collaboration and community-engaged scholarship is also highly desirable. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. DEPARTMENT DESCRIPTION: The Department of Management is a dynamic and growing unit within the Feliciano School of Business. With strengths in strategy, entrepreneurship, organizational behavior, and HR, the department is committed to preparing students for leadership in a rapidly evolving business environment. The Management curriculum emphasizes innovation, collaboration, and the application of theory to real-world challenges. The department offers a BS in Business Administration with concentrations in Management, Entrepreneurship, and Strategic Human Capital Management, a minor in Entrepreneurship, two graduate certificate programs in Human Resources Management and Project Management, as well as three undergraduate certificate programs in Entrepreneurship, Innovation Design, and Neuroinclusive Practice and Leadership. The department also supports the MBA Program and the MS in Human Resources Analytics program, teaching both required (core and concentration-specific) and elective graduate courses. Enrollment in management programs has strengthened in recent years as students increasingly seek coursework in leadership, organizational change, technology, analytics, and the future of work. The department supports this interest through new program development, strong industry partnerships, and faculty who blend scholarly rigor with practical relevance. SCHOOL DESCRIPTION The Feliciano School of Business is committed to transforming today’s students into tomorrow’s business leaders through innovative teaching, experiential learning, and strong industry engagement. Accredited by AACSB International, the School offers distinctive programs at both the undergraduate and graduate programs, including the BS in Business Analytics, BS in Business Administration (eight concentrations), BS in Accounting, BA in Economics, BA in Hospitality, Sports, Events and Tourism, MBA, MS in Accounting, MS in Business Analytics, MS in Digital Marketing Analytics, and MS in Human Resource Analytics, as well as a range of minors and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Among the School’s strengths are its world-class faculty and staff, diverse and driven student body, engaged alumni network, and strong corporate and institutional partnerships. Both academic and program-related activities are focused on student success and experiential learning beyond the classroom. The Ellyn A. McColgan Center for Student Services further supports students through results-driven advising, career guidance, and access to internships, co-ops, and mentorship opportunities that help prepare them for success in today’s dynamic business environment. The School is also home to the Feliciano Center for Entrepreneurship + Innovation, a collaborative community that supports innovation and entrepreneurship through mentorship, strategic guidance, and opportunities that help students and entrepreneurs develop and grow their ideas. Nearly 120 full-time faculty members and 41 professional staff, with terminal degrees and advanced training from leading universities, bring a wealth of academic and industry expertise to the School.   QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Significant record of scholarly publications. A PhD in Management, I/O Psychology, Organizational Behavior, Strategy, Human Resource Management, or a closely related discipline is required by the start date. Research agenda that addresses organizational change, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, or related technology-enabled changes in management. Evidence of or potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. STARTING DATE         August 27, 2027 (Pending confirmation from the Registrar’s Office)     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process. Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $130,000.00-$160,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Management Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology--Biomedical-Science_R1005051": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology, Biomedical Science",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Biology at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor in Biomedical Science . We seek an outstanding scholar and educator who will establish an innovative, externally funded research program involving undergraduate and graduate students, demonstrate excellence in teaching across the biology curriculum, and contribute to the department's strong tradition of collegiality, service, and student success. The successful candidate will join a dynamic and collaborative department within a growing R2 institution committed to inclusive excellence, interdisciplinary research, and innovation in science education. Teaching could include courses in introductory cell and molecular biology, advanced molecular biology, genetics, or courses in other areas developed by the successful candidate. These courses will support graduate and undergraduate students in the biology degree program tracks.   All research areas in cell and molecular biology will be considered, with a preferred emphasis on biomedical research using both standard and innovative organismal models. We seek candidates who are interdisciplinary, collaborative, and student-centric. As a Biology Department that integrates the work of ecology, physiology, and cell/molecular researchers, we welcome multidisciplinary research approaches. The involvement of undergraduate and graduate students in research is a priority, including a mentoring approach providing fundamental training in the process of science. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching :   The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.    Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  DEPARTMENT OF BIOLOGY The Department of Biology at Montclair State University is a leader in authentic, research-driven learning experiences, providing students with hands-on opportunities to explore biological sciences from molecular biology to ecosystems biology. We maintain a unique balance between providing a small-school feel while educating a large, diverse student body through a strong emphasis on excellent teaching and mentoring, supported by a team of professional advisors dedicated to student success. The department fosters a collaborative culture among its 24 faculty members, supporting interdisciplinary research and teaching innovation. Innovative initiatives include the SEA-PHAGES program, a Howard Hughes Medical Institute-supported project that enables students to conduct authentic research on soil-borne viruses from their first year. Students benefit from field-based learning opportunities that extend from the local environment of New Jersey to locations as far as the Galapagos. Cutting-edge laboratory courses integrate the latest technologies, allowing students to address real-world biological questions. The department is actively developing interdisciplinary degree programs, including a new BA in Biology and collaborations in Neuroscience and Biotechnology to ensure that our graduates develop a deep understanding of biological systems and current scientific methods, and adopt a critical-thinking mindset that will prepare them for diverse career pathways. We are deeply committed to fostering an environment that supports success for all students and to creating a community where staff, faculty, and students feel welcome. The Department of Biology works closely with the Health Careers Program, offering pathways for students to thrive in health-related fields. We prioritize creating a welcoming and supportive community where every student can succeed.  THE COLLEGE OF SCIENCE AND MATHEMATICS The College of Science and Mathematics at Montclair State University empowers the next generation of STEM leaders through rigorous academics, hands-on discovery, and inclusive excellence. Our mission is grounded in a student-centered philosophy that values the dedication of our faculty, the curiosity of our students, and a shared commitment to advancing scientific knowledge and innovation. With modern facilities and cutting-edge technology, we offer distinctive undergraduate and graduate programs across the Departments of Biology, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Earth and Environmental Studies, Mathematics, and Physics and Astronomy, and the School of Computing. Through a research-driven curriculum, community-engaged learning, and real-world problem-solving experiences, CSAM equips students with durable skill sets to meet the demands of an evolving world. By cultivating strong partnerships with industry, government, and nonprofit organizations, the College drives economic growth, advances environmental sustainability, and strengthens the STEM workforce across New Jersey and beyond. QUALIFICATIONS A Ph.D. in molecular biology, cell biology, or a related biomedical field. Demonstrated excellence in teaching is required, as evidenced by peer/student evaluations and/or other materials, particularly in appropriate specialty and introductory-level biology courses. A track record of recent research publications is required, along with a history of successful grant activity. SALARY RANGE      Commensurate with experience     STARTING DATE     August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  -Cover letter   -Teaching statement   -Research statement   -Curriculum vitae -Representative publications or working papers (combined into a single file) -Names and contact information of three professional references  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply three letters of recommendation. APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $80,309.12-$116,469.62 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Biology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Open-Rank-Tenure-Track-Faculty-Position--Collaborative-Keyboard_R1005030": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty Position, Collaborative Keyboard",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION: The John J. Cali School of Music at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Collaborative Keyboard at the open rank. We seek an accomplished and imaginative artist-educator who will contribute equally through excellent teaching and mentorship, an active program of performance and creative or scholarly inquiry, and collaborative leadership within the School. The successful candidate will join a vibrant, student-centered community in which performers, educators, composers, scholars, therapists, producers, and creative partners work across disciplines to advance artistic excellence and prepare students for meaningful, adaptable careers in music. This position offers an opportunity to shape the future of collaborative keyboard at the Cali School while maintaining an active professional profile and developing innovative learning and performance opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The successful candidate will teach and coach undergraduate and graduate students in areas aligned with their expertise and the needs of the School. In addition to offering Keyboard area courses, responsibilities may include chamber music coaching, vocal coaching for opera and musical theatre, private keyboard instruction, and collaboration with vocal and instrumental ensembles. The faculty member will advise and mentor students, support recruitment and auditions, and foster an inclusive learning environment that develops versatile, collaborative, and professionally prepared musicians. In addition, the successful candidate will provide artistic and administrative leadership for collaborative keyboard activities across the Cali School. Responsibilities may include coordinating collaborative assignments, contributing to curriculum and program development, supporting instructional faculty and collaborative artists, strengthening concerts and interdisciplinary projects, and helping to develop equitable and sustainable processes for the School’s extensive performance activities. The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of performance, research, and creative or scholarly activity appropriate to a tenure-track appointment. This work may include collaborative performance, recording, coaching, interdisciplinary projects, residencies, conference presentations, publications, or other forms of artistic and intellectual contribution. The faculty member will be encouraged to connect professional practice with student learning and to build collaborations across the School, University, and broader cultural community. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. THE JOHN J. CALI SCHOOL OF MUSIC: The John J. Cali School of Music offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in music education, music performance, music therapy, theory/composition, jazz studies, and recording arts and production, as well as a two-year Artist's Diploma and one-year Performer's Certificate. The Cali School collaborates with the Theater and Dance Department to provide voice instruction for students in the nationally recognized BFA Musical Theater program. Twenty-one full-time faculty members (fourteen of whom are tenured) and approximately 200 part-time instructors serve more than 500 students, who matriculate through a competitive admissions process. The school maintains strong relationships with professional performance and educational organizations along with several music schools around the world, and in the 21-22 Academic Year launched two major new initiatives with the Cali Pathways Project, focused on reducing barriers for burgeoning musicians in under-resourced communities, and the Cali Immersive Residency program, embedding world-renowned artists and ensembles for week-long residencies at the school. Its facilities provide a conservatory-like setting, consisting of the 235-seat Jed Leshowitz Recital Hall, teaching studios, music practice and rehearsal rooms, and faculty studios. Our students and faculty engage in over 300 concerts and recitals each year. THE COLLEGE OF THE ARTS: The College of the Arts (CART) at Montclair State University is a dynamic, collaborative, and inspiring community. With more than 40 undergraduate and graduate programs across the Department of Art & Design, the John J. Cali School of Music, and the Department of Theatre and Dance, CART is a vibrant hub of creativity and innovation. Over 2,000 diverse and talented students bring our state-of-the-art studios, stages, and classrooms to life every day, supported by passionate academic advisors and a career services team dedicated to their success. Programs are rigorous, creative, and designed to meet the needs of all students while offering rich opportunities for experiential learning, performance, and internships. Our faculty is a powerhouse of working composers, designers, actors, musicians, choreographers, conductors, fine artists, scholars, and professionals – Fulbright, Guggenheim, and Howard Award recipients among them – who shape the next generation through close mentorship and hands-on learning. The College is also home to the University Art Galleries, Arts and Cultural Programming, and Broadcast and Media Operations, anchoring deep connections with corporate and arts partners. Whether on campus or in the broader community, CART pulses with energy, excellence, and the belief that the arts can transform lives. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: ●    Earned appropriate terminal degree in music or a related field, or possess equivalent distinguished professional experience. ●    Record of achievement and/or potential for future success in research, scholarship, or creative activity. ●    Demonstrated excellence in teaching a broad range of students. ●    Demonstrated professional achievement and/or potential in collaborative performance. ●    A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: ●    Significant record of scholarly/creative work with clear potential for a distinguished career as a performing artist, educator, and/or scholar at both national and international levels ●    Strong background in program development, including student recruitment, concert planning, and artistic leadership ●    Experience working across a variety of musical disciplines and genres. ●    Proficiency in lyric diction in several languages. ●    Strong artistic, organizational, and interpersonal skills. STARTING DATE: August 27, 2027    REQUIRED MATERIALS: ●    Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications where applicable (publications may include commercial recordings, concert programs, and/or scholarly books and articles), which can be uploaded during the application process. ●    Links to recent recordings of at least two collaborative performances, rehearsals, masterclasses, or other relevant collaborative activity. ●    Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY:    The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately.  Applications received by October 16, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Questions may be addressed to the search chair, Prof. Aaron Helgeson, at helgesona@montclair.edu. Salary Range $80,309.12-$136,463.80 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Cali School of Music Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Senior-Repairer--Multiple-Posiitons-_R1004774": {
      "title": "Senior Repairer (Multiple Posiitons)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Crew Supervisor or other Supervisor associated with a specific Facilities Maintenance & Engineering Trade Shop, the Senior Repairer performs a variety of routine basic maintenance and repair tasks involved with carpentry, painting, plumbing, steam fitting, electrical and mechanical; and provides first rate customer service to the University Community. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : As a team leader or working independently, work in the painting of wood, metal, brick and cement walls, floors, and ceilings of the interior and exterior of buildings; the staining, varnishing and refinishing of cabinets, desks, chairs and other furnishings and equipment; and the painting and repainting of pipes, radiators, tin roofs, and other types of iron work. As a team leader or working independently, work in the repair and maintenance of walls, ceilings, interior and exterior brickwork, tile floors, drains, cement and concrete floors, sidewalks, steps, foundations, and other types of masonry, plastering and stone work. As a team leader or working independently, work in the repair and maintenance of water, drainage, waste and gas lines; toilet bowls, wash basins, and urinals; and radiators, refrigerators, laundry machines and other types of plumbing and steamfitting fixtures, fittings, appliances and machinery. As a team leader or working independently, work in the repair and maintenance of buildings, office furniture, screens, storm sashes, frames, windows, ceilings, partitions, and other types of carpentry work. As a team leader or working independently, work in the installation, inspection, repair, and maintenance of cables, wiring, motor, generators, pumps, refrigerators, radios, sound equipment, telephone line switchboard, oil burners, and other type of electrical equipment, appliance fixtures, machinery, and circuits. As a team leader or working independently, work in the repair and maintenance of copper leaders, gutters and slate roofs, including the operations of flashing, papering, cutting and punching prior to the installation of slate; pots, steamers, cans, pails, and other kitchen and dairy equipment; and ventilators, air duct, and weatherproofing equipment. As a team leader or working independently, work in the cleaning and repair of boilers, the repairing of locks, and the repair and maintenance of automobiles, trucks, snow plow, and sand spreaders. Perform welding and/or brazing operations to repair furniture or equipment. Assign work and supervise performance of unskilled and semi-skilled maintenance, repair and laboring work of a helper. Perform duties on all buildings on campus and all exterior features on campus. Use work orders and fill in all pertinent information. Follow all safety procedures including wearing uniform and appropriate protective personal equipment. Ensure that all staff and customers are treated with respect and courtesy. All customers to be greeted, questioned as to their needs, advised of any necessary information and thanked for their business in a pleasant manner. Staff is to be treated similarly. Utilize various types of electronic and/or manual recording and computerized management information systems used by the Facilities Maintenance & Engineering. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Two (2) years of experience in work involving the inspection, repair and general maintenance of household, office and other equipment, fixtures, fittings, appliances, machinery, furnishings, and buildings. Appointees will be required to possess a driver’s license valid in New Jersey only if the operation of the vehicle rather than employee mobility, is necessary to perform the essential duties of the position. Knowledge of standard tools, materials and methods. Ability to work with diverse populations and in a team. Ability to understand and follow safety procedures. Ability to read, speak and understand English sufficiently to perform duties of this position. Availability to work all shifts, including weekends and holidays. PREFERRED : Ability to analyze/trouble shoot problems. High School Diploma or GED certificate. *NOTE: This is a Civil Service position.  As required by the State of New Jersey, in order to be certified to the position and attain permanent status in title, candidates are subject to an examination process and successful completion of a 4-Month Working Test Period. This position is designated as essential. The designation of essential requires employees at these 24/7 facilities to be present due to inclement weather situations. This position requires on campus work and is not a position that allows remote work. SALARY RANGE : O14: $46,295.93 -$67,001.13 *NOTE : Salaries for internal candidates are determined by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission’s formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step four, $52,507.49. Salary Range $46,295.93-$52,507.49 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department General Mechanics Position Type Services Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Grounds-Worker--Multiple-Positions-_R1005018": {
      "title": "Grounds Worker (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-04\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Assistant Head Grounds Worker, the Grounds Worker performs tasks that result in horticultural sound practices leading to first-rate care of the University's landscape. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Monitor campus grounds to determine needs for services such as but not limited to: fertilizing, insect and disease control, weeding, dead plant removal, watering, pruning, etc. Police campus grounds and pick up litter and debris on an as needed basis. Maintain lawns and softscapes to maintain a neat and horticultural appealing appearance. This includes the following services: mowing, trimming, edging and other activities. Water new plant material and floral displays to help with establishment and survival. Prune trees and shrubs according to University policy to maintain their health and aesthetic value as well as to maintain street, walkway, building, signage and lighting clearance. Install and maintain seasonal plantings using annual flowers, perennial flowers, ornamental grasses, bulbs, etc. Remove snow and ice via the use of truck/plow, ATV/plow, snow blower, shovel, etc. in order to maintain safe roadways, sidewalks, and stairways on the campus. Report to supervisor the need for any services or any unsafe action and/or condition. Place a premium upon safety rules and regulations pertaining to operation of tools, machinery, etc. Maintain and prepare athletic fields and adjacent areas for practices and events, including but not limited to: dragging, vacuuming, lining, clean-up, etc. Edge, cultivate, and mulch tree rings and shrub beds. Remove leaves from lawns, walks, roads, parking lots, etc. on an as needed basis to maintain a clean and safe environment. Inspect, clean, and perform preventive maintenance of equipment and tools used in the performance of tasks. Prepare areas to be landscaped and install landscape material as required (examples include soil, seed, sod, mulch, shrubs, trees, pavers, decorative stone, etc.). Build skill base by attending landscape training sessions as assigned. Attend safety training as identified by the leadership of the Grounds department. Acquire knowledge of and utilize technology as required to fulfill duties (examples include handheld devices, pagers, two-way radios, cellphones, etc.). Respond to emergencies and close out assigned work order requests in a timely and professional manner. Treat customers, coworkers, students and guests with respect. Provide supervisor with a log that indicates activities completed on a particular day. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS :  REQUIRED : One year of experience in the performance of landscape maintenance work. A valid NJ Driver's license. Ability to read, write, speak, understand or communicate in English sufficiently to perform the duties of the position. Must be available to work all shifts, overtime, and holidays. PREFERRED : Two years of experience in large-scale operation and maintenance of grounds, gardens, and/or sports fields. New Jersey Commercial Pesticide Applicators License with certifications in categories 3A and 3B and ProFACT fertilizer license. *NOTE: This is a Civil Service position.  As required by the State of New Jersey, in order to be certified to the position and attain permanent status in title, candidates are required to successfully serve a 4-Month Working Test Period. This position is designated as essential. The designation of essential requires employees at these 24/7 facilities to be present due to inclement weather situations. This position requires on campus work and is not a position that allows remote work.  SALARY RANGE: O10: $40,321.62 - $57,948.52 *NOTE : Salaries for internal candidates are determined by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission’s formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step four, $45,609.69. NJ SAME Applicants This position is a non-competitive, unclassified posting and complies with the NJ SAME Program. If you are applying under the New Jersey \"SAME\" program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B letter), resume (CV), as well as the names and contact information for three professional references should also be sent to: same@montclair.edu and hrcompliance@montclair.edu   For more information on the SAME program visit their website at: https://nj.gov/csc/same/overview/index.shtml , email: SAME@csc.nj.gov , or call CSC at: 833-691-0404. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act P.L. 2011 c.70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees in certain positions (other than faculty who are exempt) are required to obtain New Jersey residency within one (1) year of employment. Applicants who have a concern with meeting this requirement should discuss with Human Resources if the position for which they have applied is eligible for an exemption from this requirement. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $40,321.62-$57,948.52 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Grounds Services 3 Position Type Services Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Employer-Relations-Specialist--College-of-Science-and-Mathematics-_R1005017": {
      "title": "Employer Relations Specialist (College of Science and Mathematics)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-30\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of Career Services in the College of Science and Mathematics (CSAM), the Employer Relations Specialist will develop and implement employer engagement strategies, cultivate employer partnerships, and coordinate and secure resources to support career-related programs that expand student access to internships, cooperative education, and career opportunities. Success in this role requires independent judgment, strong collaboration skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities from inception to completion. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and implement employer engagement strategies aligned with college and institutional priorities. Build, manage, and strategically grow relationships with employer partners to expand and sustain pipelines for internships, cooperative education, and career opportunities. Conduct employer site visits to deepen partnerships and increase experiential learning opportunities. Partner with employers to design branding and marketing strategies that maximize student engagement. Design, plan, and execute employer engagement programs and events, including career fairs, networking events, and site visits, with responsibility for outcomes and continuous improvement. Operate with a high level of independence and accountability, exercising professional judgment while collaborating with stakeholders and leadership to advance unit and institutional goals. Collaborate with CSAM departments and university career services staff to align employer engagement efforts across colleges/schools. Analyze employer engagement metrics, student participation, and program outcomes to inform strategy, improve effectiveness, and guide decision-making. Maintain current knowledge of workforce and industry trends, particularly within science and mathematics fields. Ensure events are executed with strong attention to detail from planning through post-event assessment. Review, approve, and manage job postings in Handshake. Leverage platforms such as Handshake, LinkedIn, and Montclair Connect to promote opportunities and engage stakeholders. Lead and contribute to marketing and communication strategies that promote employer partnerships and student engagement. Uphold university policies related to employer engagement and student services, including FERPA. Represent the department at university events and serve on committees as appropriate. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Master's degree from accredited college or university in higher education, counseling, career services, business, science, and mathematics-related fields, or a closely related discipline. Minimum of three years of experience in career services, employer relations, recruitment, or event coordination. Demonstrated ability to build and sustain strategic relationships with employers and external partners. Strong communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively across all organizational levels. Proven ability to manage multiple priorities and independently coordinate complex initiatives, including employer engagement and large-scale events. Proficiency in career services platforms and technology tools (e.g., Handshake, LinkedIn, Zoom, Microsoft Office, Google Workspace). Experience utilizing data to inform outreach strategies, assess program effectiveness, and support continuous improvement. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments and with external partners. Flexibility to support occasional evening and weekend programming. PREFERRED: Experience developing and implementing employer engagement strategies in a higher education setting, particularly with STEM-focused organizations. Experience analyzing recruitment, engagement, or program data to inform decision-making and improve outcomes. Familiarity with science and mathematics career pathways and experiential learning opportunities (internships, cooperative education, research placements). PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.   Salary Range $76,486.40-$87,954.55 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department CSAM Career Services Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Building-Maintenance-Worker_R1004657": {
      "title": "Building Maintenance Worker (Housekeeper) (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-07-28\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Crew Supervisor and/or Assistant Housekeeping Supervisor, the Building Maintenance Worker is responsible for maintaining cleanliness of the Montclair State University Facilities. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Clean campus facilities alone or in teams; clean public areas and meeting spaces. Perform room set-ups; replace light bulbs, clean light fixtures and restrooms. Sweep, mop, strip and wax, buff floors; vacuum and shampoo carpets. Collect and remove trash, bring trash to curb or receptacles, transfer recyclable materials. Dust all surface and vent, and clean inside window surfaces. Clean desks, tables, chairs, and remove graffiti. Clean offices, classrooms, and work areas. Perform snow removal as directed. Attend in-service training and participate in University quality and processing improvement initiatives. Assist with the sorting, distribution, transportation and storage of cleaning supplies. Keep janitorial closet stocked and clean; maintain housekeeping equipment. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Ability to speak, read, and understand English. Ability to lift 25 lbs. and use a ladder. Ability to work any shift, overtime and holidays in the performance of assigned responsibilities. PREFERRED : A high school diploma or its equivalency. Housekeeping experience in a university, school or hospital setting. *NOTE: This is a Civil Service position.  As required by the State of New Jersey, in order to be certified to the position and attain permanent status in title, candidates are required to successfully serve a 4-Month Working Test Period. This position is designated as essential. The designation of essential requires employees at these 24/7 facilities to be present due to inclement weather situations. This position requires on campus work and is not a position that allows remote work.         SALARY RANGE: O09: $38,640.95 - $55,447.65 *NOTE: Salaries for internal candidates are determined by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission’s formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step four, $43,682.96. NJ SAME Applicants This position is a non-competitive, unclassified posting and complies with the NJ SAME Program. If you are applying under the New Jersey \"SAME\" program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B letter), resume (CV), as well as the names and contact information for three professional references should also be sent to: same@montclair.edu and hrcompliance@montclair.edu For more information on the SAME program visit their website at: https://nj.gov/csc/same/overview/index.shtml , email: SAME@csc.nj.gov , or call CSC at: 833-691-0404. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act P.L. 2011 c.70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees in certain positions (other than faculty who are exempt) are required to obtain New Jersey residency within one (1) year of employment. Applicants who have a concern with meeting this requirement should discuss with Human Resources if the position for which they have applied is eligible for an exemption from this requirement. Salary Range $18.58-$26.66 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Housekeeping Services/Acad. 4 Position Type Services Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
