    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Academic-Success-Advisor--Online-Business-Programs_R1005134": {
      "title": "Academic Success Advisor, Online Business Programs",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY Reporting to the Assistant Director of Academic Advising, the Academic Success Advisor, Online Business Programs provides academic advising and ongoing academic success support to an assigned caseload of students enrolled in the Feliciano School of Business (SBUS) online programs. The advisor supports students from initial enrollment through graduation by utilizing academic planning strategies, proactive outreach, and individualized coaching. The advisor also collaborates with the Ellyn A. McColgan Student Services Center, Montclair Unbound, faculty, and University offices to address barriers to academic progress and continued enrollment. The position serves students with varied educational backgrounds and responsibilities, including adult learners, transfer students, and students returning to college.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide academic advising on course selection, registration, degree requirements, prerequisites, and graduation planning for an assigned online student caseload. Assist in the development and updating of academic plans that reflect students’ degree progress, goals, and responsibilities; communicate changes in curriculum and academic policies. Support incoming and transfer students through onboarding and initial registration; explain how evaluated transfer credits apply to their programs and coordinate questions with appropriate offices. Assist in outreach at key points in the term, including registration deadlines; follow up with nonregistered students and those considering stopping out. Monitor academic progress and respond to faculty referrals and academic alerts; help students on probation or with conditional admission requirements develop improvement plans. Advocate for online students navigating university services; coordinate with Admissions, Red Hawk Central, the Registrar, and other offices to resolve barriers to academic progress. Refer students to tutoring, accessibility services, counseling, career development, and other resources; follow up when unresolved concerns affect continued enrollment. Deliver virtual advising and communications; help students navigate online learning resources and refer technical issues to appropriate support staff. Maintain accurate advising notes, outreach records, and follow-up plans in Banner, Degree Works, Navigate, Workday Student and other approved systems; protect student information. Participate in SBUS Career Fairs, Open Houses, On-campus recruitment, New Student Orientations, Transfer Orientations, Accepted Students Days, Campus to Career Transitions events, Commencements and other events as requested. Assist in the development of virtual orientation activities, workshops, and accessible advising resources tailored to online students. Collaborate with Unbound staff, faculty, and academic support colleagues to coordinate services and contribute to improvements in online student support. Assist in the analysis of caseload progress, registration, and engagement with support services; assist in preparation of reports and recommend improvements based on student needs and outcomes. Participate in recruitment, orientation, and engagement activities relevant to online programs, along with Business School meetings, committees, and other events as assigned. Maintain current knowledge of online advising and academic coaching practices. Perform other duties as assigned. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university. A minimum of two years of experience working in a higher education setting or similar organization. Ability to interpret academic requirements and university policies and provide individualized guidance to students from diverse backgrounds. Strong interpersonal, written, and virtual communication skills and ability to build effective relationships with students and campus partners. Ability to use student information systems and virtual communication tools, maintain accurate records, and use data to guide outreach and follow-up. Excellent organizational skills; ability to manage a caseload, prioritize responsibilities, and work independently and collaboratively. Ability to work periodic evening and weekend hours to support students and program activities. PREFERRED: Experience supporting online, adult, transfer, or returning college students. Experience with academic coaching, proactive outreach, and retention initiatives; understanding of student development theory. Familiarity with business curricula, online learning platforms, Banner, Degree Works, Navigate and Workday Student. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $66,067.40-$72,679.50 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Feliciano School of Business/Academic Services Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Associate-Director-of-Residential-Education_R1005044": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Residential Education",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of Residential Education, the Associate Director of Residential Education is responsible for coordinating all activities, programs, as well as training, selection and development for all student staff lines for the Department. The Department is responsible for more than 5,500 students residing in various apartment and residential communities on two campuses, including two complexes maintained through a joint effort with Capstone On Campus Management. The Associate Director of Residential Education collaborates with University Campus partners to assist in the creation of a seamless residential experience for residents. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: ● Supervise the Residential Student Support Specialist and Graduate Program Coordinator, and indirect oversight of 330 student employees. ● Lead student staff hiring, training, and development for all academic year and summer student staff positions. ● Develop and implement learning objectives, manuals, and training programs for student staff positions. ● Coordinate logistics for training events, speakers, and development activities. ● Oversee recruitment processes including interview design, scoring rubrics, and hiring workflows. ● Maintain the student staff roster and manage onboarding in collaboration with Human Resources. ● Evaluate performance of student staff through structured tools. ● Support student governance, including Residence Hall Associations and councils in collaboration with Assistant Directors and live-on professional staff. ● Collaborate with campus partners to enhance the residential living experience. ● Develop, monitor and evaluate the residential curriculum and make annual improvements. ● Support Assistant Directors and Graduate Program Coordinator in compiling programming metrics and reports. ● Maintain programming inventory and recommend long-term supply purchases. ● Create promotional materials and maintain proficiency in relevant software tools. ● Lead department co-sponsorship initiatives and other programming in partnership with campus offices. ● Assist with residence hall opening/closing, special events, and weekend programming as needed. ● Serve as on-call administrator for residential life emergencies. ● Represent the department on inter- and intra-departmental committees. ● Demonstrate professional ethics, initiative, and engagement in departmental meetings. ● Management retains the right to change or add job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS: REQUIRED: ● Masters degree from accredited college or university in higher education administration, student personnel services or related field. ● A minimum of six years of professional residence life or student affairs experience with a record of progressive advancement and supervision. ● Excellent time management skills plus a strong proficiency in written and oral communication. ● Direct experience with professional and student staff supervision, training and development, residence hall activities and educational programs. PREFERRED: ● Experience working with multicultural groups. ● Live-in experience. ● Knowledge of college student development, programmatic needs, and fostering a sense of belonging. ● Working knowledge of project management methodologies and a desire to improve efficiency, quality, and customer satisfaction with a focus on continuous improvement. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $87,500.00-$88,580.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Residential Life Education Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Director-of-Classification-and-Compensation_R1005138": {
      "title": "Director of Classification and Compensation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Associate Vice President, Human Resources Operations, the Director of Classification and Compensation leads Montclair State University’s classification, compensation, and job architecture programs for a workforce of more than 6,600 full- and part-time employees spanning civil service, unclassified, managerial, and multiple collective bargaining units. As head of the Classification and Compensation Center of Expertise, the Director sets direction for how the University values its jobs, puts the University’s Compensation Philosophy into practice, and ensures that every classification and pay decision is timely, defensible, equitable, and clearly explained.   The Director is accountable for both the strategy and the service: building a market-informed job architecture and salary structure while running a high-volume, deadline-driven operation with published standards, reliable data, and a capable, accountable team. The Director is the University’s principal advisor on compensation to senior leadership and works closely with HR Business Partners, Budget and Planning, Employee and Labor Relations, Payroll, and HR Operations.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Set the University’s Compensation Philosophy into practice and recommend updates as institutional priorities and market conditions change. Design, maintain, and periodically review the University’s job architecture (job families, functions, levels, and career paths) and salary structures for applicable employee groups, using a defined peer set and a documented market-pricing methodology (e.g., CUPA-HR, NJASCU, and R2 peer data). Lead periodic pay equity analyses consistent with New Jersey equal pay requirements; recommend and cost remediation. Ensure salary ranges included in job postings meet New Jersey pay transparency requirements and are consistent with approved structures. Model the cost of compensation actions, reclassifications, structure adjustments, salary increase programs, and contract proposals, in partnership with Budget and Planning. Provide compensation analysis and costing to support collective bargaining and contract administration in partnership with Labor Relations. Direct classification, reclassification, title change, promotion, and organizational restructuring reviews, including desk audits, position evaluation, and internal and external benchmarking; serve as final departmental reviewer of recommendations. Interpret and administer New Jersey Civil Service Commission requirements, including Title 4A, across the civil service employee lifecycle; serves as the University’s working liaison to the Civil Service Commission on classification matters. Administer the classification and compensation provisions of collective bargaining agreements, including the professional staff performance-based promotion process, and ensure contractual deadlines are met to prevent retroactive pay liability. Maintain a consistent, documented job evaluation methodology so that comparable requests produce comparable, defensible outcomes. Ensure job descriptions and position records are accurate, current, and maintained in the system of record. Establish and publish service standards and turnaround targets for each request type, and holds the unit accountable to them. Maintain a case tracking process that provides real-time visibility into the status, ownership, and age of every request; conduct regular backlog and aging reviews and take documented corrective action. Report regularly to HR leadership on volume, turnaround, aging, outcomes, and cost; contribute classification and compensation metrics to division, annual, and Board of Trustees reporting. Own classification and compensation business processes, position management, and compensation data integrity in Workday; identify and lead automation and process improvement. Maintain standard operating procedures and cross-training so that service continues without reliance on any single individual. Serve as the principal compensation advisor to the President’s Cabinet, deans, and division leaders, and as the escalation point for HR Business Partners on complex classification and organizational design questions. Build pay literacy across the University through plain-language guidance, manager toolkits, and workshops explaining how jobs are classified, how pay is set, and how reclassification and promotion work. Communicate decisions clearly and promptly to employees, managers, and union representatives; escalate complex, sensitive, or high-risk matters appropriately. Coordinate annual classification, reclassification, reappointment, and promotion calendars with Learning and Talent Development, Employee and Labor Relations, and Academic Affairs. Lead, coach, and develop the Classification and Compensation team; set clear performance expectations, distribute work equitably, and monitor quality and productivity. Build analyst capability and bench strength aligned with the HR division’s Capability Development Framework. Address performance gaps promptly and in accordance with University procedures and applicable agreements. Model the service culture and partnership expectations of the HR division. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in human resources, business administration, public administration, finance, or a related field. Minimum of five years of progressively responsible classification and compensation experience, including job evaluation, market pricing, and salary structure design or administration. Minimum of three years supervising professional staff, with demonstrated accountability for team performance, workload, and service outcomes. Experience in a unionized environment administering the classification and compensation provisions of collective bargaining agreements. New Jersey public sector experience, including Civil Service Commission and Title 4A requirements. Demonstrated success managing a high-volume operation against measurable service standards, using data to manage backlog and turnaround. Advanced analytical skills, including Excel-based modeling and cost projection, and experience with a human resources information system. Ability to explain complex compensation concepts clearly — in writing and in person — to executives, managers, employees, and union representatives. PREFERRED : Master’s degree in a relevant discipline. Higher education experience, including familiarity with CUPA-HR survey data. Experience with Workday HCM compensation, position management, and reporting. Experience leading a job architecture build, salary structure redesign, or pay equity study. Certified Compensation Professional (CCP); SHRM-SCP or SPHR. Experience presenting to senior leadership or a governing board. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $150,000.00-$170,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department HR Operations Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Director-of-IT-Communications_R1005131": {
      "title": "Director of IT Communications",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Deputy Chief Information Officer, the Director of Information Technology Communications is a strategic leadership role responsible for shaping the narrative of technology’s impact across the university. This position bridges the gap between complex technical initiatives and the diverse needs of students, faculty, and staff. The Director designs and leads a comprehensive communications program that enhances the IT department's transparency, promotes digital literacy, and manages critical messaging during service interruptions or cybersecurity events. The position is responsible for the development and publishing of timely, accurate and well written information technology centric communications across multiple internal and external platforms and avenues (e.g. email, web content, social media, etc.). These communications inform key stakeholders of important changes, plans and events they must be aware of for them to prepare for upcoming changes, initiatives and responses to planned and unplanned campus technology use.  The Director is a primary leader in planning new communications, crafting and publishing incident response information and ensuring that the communication takes multiple paths to reach and be understood by essential audiences.     PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and execute an annual integrated communications plan that aligns with the University’s strategic goals and the IT department's roadmap. Oversee the \"IT Brand,\" ensuring all digital and print materials—from the service portal to departmental newsletters—maintain a consistent, professional, and accessible voice. Serve as the lead communicator during IT outages, security breaches, or campus-wide transitions. Develop communications that translate technical jargon into clear, actionable instructions for non-technical users under high-pressure timelines. Produce high-quality content including executive presentations, annual reports, campus-wide emails, social media updates, and \"success stories\" highlighting ITs role in supporting the University. Translate technical technology materials into accessible and friendly campus community communications, guides and publications. Use best judgement, informed decision making and best practices to successfully and appropriately navigate unique demands and cultural landscape of a large, modern public university. Partner with IT leaders and subject matter experts to develop compelling award nominations, case studies, and supporting materials that highlight strategic initiatives and measurable business outcomes. Effectively transition from long-term communication campaigns to timely emergency “system down” alerts as required. Partner with University stakeholders, including but not limited to Communications, Student Affairs, and Faculty organizations to ensure IT initiatives are socialized effectively before, during and after rollout. Manage the IT department’s website and internal knowledge base, prioritizing User Experience (UX) and Accessibility (ADA compliance). Own the enterprise incident communications function, ensuring clear, timely, and consistent communications during technology incidents, cyber events, and service disruptions in alignment with incident management and crisis response processes. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time.   QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED: Bachelor’s degree from accredited college or university A minimum of five years of experience in professional communications, with at least 3 years in a technical or higher education environment. Ability to understand and explain complex concepts like Cloud Computing, Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA), and Research Computing.   PREFERRED: Experience using CMS platforms (e.g., Drupal, WordPress). Proficiency in graphic design tools (Adobe Creative Suite or Canva). Familiarity with IT Service Management (ITSM) tools like ServiceNow. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $125,000.00-$140,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Office of the Deputy CIO Information Technology Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/JobOpportunities/job/Montclair-NJ/Vice-President-for-Student-Development-and-Campus-Life_R1005159": {
      "title": "Vice President for Student Development and Campus Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-30\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description THE OPPORTUNITY :   Montclair State University is building the model of a public-serving university. At its core is a commitment to access and excellence that centers students and their success.  Unlike the traditional model of higher education, Montclair believes that the experiences outside the classroom are as pivotal to the university experience as the academic environment. As such we seek to create a vibrant, engaging, safe and supportive environment characterized by a strong sense of belonging and community that provides a setting where students can develop interpersonal skills, challenge each other, gain leadership experience and build relationships.   Montclair seeks an innovative and collaborative leader to serve as its next Vice President for Student Development and Campus Life who will take the lead in developing and growing  this dynamic environment. Reporting to the President and serving as a member of the University’s Executive Council, the Vice President provides strategic and operational leadership for a comprehensive portfolio dedicated to advancing student success, engagement, belonging, health and well-being, safety, leadership development, and the overall student experience across two campuses.   The Vice President will provide vision and direction for the Division of Student Development and Campus Life, fostering an integrated approach to the student experience and ensuring that programs and services are responsive to the needs of Montclair’s diverse student population. The Vice President will serve as a trusted advisor to the President and a strategic partner to the academic and administrative leaders across the University.    The ideal candidate will be a strategic, forward-thinking, and collaborative leader who combines vision with strong execution. This individual will bring intellectual curiosity, creativity, sound judgment and a genuine commitment to students. This leader will communicate with authenticity and empathy and inspire others to work collaboratively toward shared goals. The next Vice President will have the opportunity to build upon the strengths of a broad and talented division while shaping the future of student development and campus life at Montclair State University.    Montclair’s Student Development and Campus Life division supports students from their first experience at the University through graduation, and everything in between, which encompasses a broad range of student programs and services. Its focus is on helping students belong, engage, promote their well-being, develop leadership skills, and successfully navigate their college experience. The division is broad and touches virtually every aspect of campus life. Major areas of focus:   ·         Student Success and Advocacy ·         Student Conduct and Community Standards ·         Residential and Commuter Life ·         Student Engagement and Leadership ·         Student Belonging and Inclusion ·         Student Access and Support Services ·         Health, Wellness and Support Services ·         Campus Life, Events and Communications ·         Athletics and Recreation ·         Campus Safety and Security   The Vice President will be responsible for ensuring this broad portfolio operates as a collaborative, cohesive, strategic division with a shared focus on student success, belonging, wellness and a vibrant student experience. The Vice President will champion professional growth across the division, developing staff capabilities and cultivating leadership at all levels to build a high-performing team that supports the University’s mission. Additionally, the Vice President will be responsible for:   KEY RESPONSIBILITIES   Develop and advance a compelling and strategic vision for the Division of Student Development and Campus Life that is aligned with the University’s mission and priorities. Lead a comprehensive portfolio of student-facing programs and services that support student success, engagement, belonging, well-being, leadership development and campus life.  Strengthen an integrated and vibrant student experience across the University’s campuses and student populations.  Build strong partnerships across the University and its two campuses, while collaborating with Academic Affairs, Enrollment Management, Communications and Marketing, University Development, Human Resources and other campus partners to advance student retention, engagement and success and advance institutional priorities.  Foster an environment where students feel connected, supported, valued and empowered to achieve their educational and personal goals.  Lead and develop a high-performing division, establishing a culture of collaboration, accountability, innovation, student-centered service and continuous improvement. Ensure effective management of divisional resources, including people, financial resources and programs, to maximize impact and advance institutional goals.  Provide strategic leadership for services that support students’ mental, physical, emotional and overall well-being.  Leverage data, assessment, student perspectives and emerging trends to inform decisions and continuously improve the student experience.  Provide executive leadership in responding to complex student matters, crises, and emerging issues in collaboration with the appropriate University partners. Advance strategies that address food, housing, financial and other barriers that can interfere with student success.  Working closely with University Police and campus partners to promote a safe, welcoming and supportive environment for students, faculty, staff and visitors across both campuses.  Build and maintain strong relationships with students and families, faculty, staff, senior leaders, alumni and external partners and serve as a visible advocate for the student experience, bringing best practices and innovative approaches to student development and campus life.   QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Master’s degree from an accredited institution, preferably in higher education, student affairs, public administration or a related field.  Minimum of ten years of progressively responsible experience in student affairs or a related field, with demonstrated success in senior leadership. Experience building and leading a cohesive team while managing a broad student development and campus life portfolio in a complex and diverse higher education environment.  Demonstrated success developing and implementing strategic initiatives that enhance student success and the student experience.  Proven ability to build collaborative relationships and bring people together across organizational and functional areas.  Exceptional communication skills, including the ability to engage with diverse constituencies with credibility, empathy and discretion.  Demonstrated ability to use data, assessment and emerging trends to inform decisions, improve services and advance innovation.  Experience addressing complex student, safety, or crisis-related matters. Residency and Housing: Must reside in a university-designated residence or in close proximity to ensure a visible presence and rapid response for campus emergencies and community events; university housing is provided. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time.   PREFERRED: Doctoral degree from an accredited institution.  Demonstrated commitment to student belonging and inclusion.  Demonstrated ability to successfully plan for and lead during times of crisis. Experience working with multiple campuses. Demonstrated success leading organizational change and cross-campus initiatives.  PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $290,000.00-$330,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Office of the President Position Type Executive Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    }
  },
